  "body": "At the window's default size, a Geometry-tab selection row no longer runs past the Properties panel's edge: each row's × (remove this pick) is always on screen, and a label too long for the panel is shortened, with the whole label shown on hover.\n\n## What changed\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/geo_page.rs`, `chips`: a row was laid out as [Set origin buttons] [label] [×]. A face row's two Set origin buttons made it wider than the panel at 1280 × 800, so its label was cut off and its × was out of reach. Now:\n\n- the × comes first in the row, so it is always on screen;\n- the label takes the width that is left and is shortened with \"…\" when it doesn't fit (`egui::Label::truncate`, which shows the whole label on hover).\n\nThe row hover from #1520 is unchanged: the label, the ×, the Set origin buttons and the row's own rectangle all still light the pick in the viewport.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New: `egui_app::tests::geo_row_hover::every_rows_remove_button_is_in_reach_at_the_default_window_size`. At 1280 × 800 (`shell_window`'s default size), with a face, a chain and a vertex picked, every row's × is on screen, hovering it lights its pick, and clicking the face row's × removes the face pick. Without this change it fails: the face row's × sits at x = 1406.\n- The two existing `geo_row_hover` tests still pass, at their wide 2400 × 1000 window.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (the `camcraft-ui` lib tests and the `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `sinker_setup` and `theme_files` suites).\n- By hand in the desktop app on macOS, at the default window size, with the same three picks as the #1507 check (before / after screenshots below).\n\n**Before** (main, 1280 × 800): the face row's label is cut off and its × is past the panel edge.\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"before: face row hovered\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9c6e27a4-ae7c-490f-bdc9-7717785fb80f\" />\n\n**After:** every row's × is on the left and in reach; long labels end in \"…\".\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"after-1-rows\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/254bdfa1-c1fa-4318-8724-59d305fde1a1\" />\n\n**After:** hovering the face row's × lights its face.\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"after-2-face-x-hovered\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dee49a8e-d0c8-410d-beb2-d647fab58b6f\" />\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and Linux by hand. The layout is plain egui, with nothing per platform.\n- Very narrow panels: the × and the Set origin buttons stay in reach down to about the width of the buttons themselves, below which egui clips them as before.\n\nFork synced at v0.19.0 (process files at PROCESS_VERSION 65); this branch merges `upstream/main` because the row hover from #1520 landed after v0.19.0.\n\nChangelog: Geometry tab: a selection row's remove button stays in reach at the default window size, and a long label is shortened with the full text on hover.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1688\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
